node_modules/
# Probe fixtures are miniature install graphs (#17): their `node_modules` trees
# are the fixture and must be committed. Git cannot re-include a path beneath an
# excluded directory, so the fixture directory chain is re-included explicitly.
!packages/dependency-resolver/src/__fixtures__/probe/**/node_modules/
!packages/dependency-resolver/src/__fixtures__/probe/**/node_modules/**
dist/
coverage/
.vite/
.fgc/
*.log
.DS_Store

# One probe fixture ships a directory literally named `.fgc/`, because a package is free
# to have one and the artifact bound must not treat that name as the probe's scratch
# space. The blanket `.fgc/` rule above would drop it from the commit, so the fixture is
# re-included **after** that rule — git applies these in order, and a negation that comes
# earlier loses. Without this the fixture exists locally and is absent on CI, so the test
# passes here and fails there, which is worse than having no test at all.
!packages/dependency-resolver/src/__fixtures__/probe/dot-fgc-directory/node_modules/dot-fgc/src/.fgc/
!packages/dependency-resolver/src/__fixtures__/probe/dot-fgc-directory/node_modules/dot-fgc/src/.fgc/**
